--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 0177 attempted the Experiment 1 production sweep on 2026-05-20 and
was halted before completion. Two issues surfaced during that attempt:

1. **Silent-drop regressions in the manager+worker pipeline** introduced by
   ticket 0175 — `model_set`, `seed`, `max_tokens`, and the `modules_dir`
   default were all silently dropped. Without these, the sweep cannot
   honour the 0175 lock.
   Fixed in PR #338 (commit d7c6efe).

2. **Journal model set inconsistencies** — `qwen3-max` was paired with three
   `qwen3.6-*` siblings; user requested an Opus 4.7→4.6 swap on inspection.
   Both qwen3.6-max-preview and claude-opus-4.6 verified live on OpenRouter
   /api/v1/models 2026-05-20.
   Fixed in PR #341 (qwen3.6-max-preview added — augment, not replace) and
   PR #346 (Opus 4.7→4.6 swap + uniform `max_tokens` raise to 32768 +
   `budget_usd` raise to $15, because Opus 4.7 had hit `finish_reason=length`
   on smoke output truncated at 78 table rows).

Net result on `main` (HEAD 2d8e268, 2026-05-20 ~20:31Z):

- Journal set has **17 models × 5 reps = 85 runs** (augment kept both
  `qwen3-max` and `qwen3.6-max-preview` so Experiment 2's within-family
  thinking pair survives).
- Sweep config: `temperature=0.0`, `seed=42`, `max_tokens=32768`,
  `budget_usd=15`, `prompt_modules=[]`, `system_instruction` declares
  no-web-search.
- Output dir: `experiments/outputs/ablation/direct/p1_base/`.

## Provenance from 0177 (smoke evidence)

The 0177 attempt produced one verified-good smoke record before halting:
`mistralai/mistral-small-2603` run 1 with the patched code, recorded
`cost=$0.0026`, `wall=22.5s`, `finish_reason=stop`, 42 table rows, all four
locked knobs (`system_instruction`, `seed=42`, `max_tokens=8192`,
`temperature=0.0`) present in the saved JSON. That validates the pipeline
end-to-end; the rerun does not need to re-smoke before draining.

The 0177 attempt also surfaced **Opus 4.7 truncation at 8192 max_tokens** —
the very reason PR #346 raised the cap to 32768. Opus 4.6 is expected to
behave the same way per-call (same model family / API ceiling), so the
32768 cap is the controlled variable for the rerun.

## Actions

1. Preflight (`make -C experiments preflight`). `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` must be
   set; Tavily / Ollama / GROBID warnings are non-blocking.

2. Generate jobs from the locked sweep config:
   `uv run --project .. --env-file ../.env python -m aedist.manager generate --sweep sweep_ablation_p1_direct_base --experiments experiments.toml`
   Expected output: **85 jobs**, exactly **17 unique `model_filter` values**.
   (Anything else means PR #338 / #341 / #346 regressed — STOP.)

3. Drain in parallel. Use 4 OpenRouter workers (8 is the upper bound but
   4 keeps per-batch cost visibility cleaner given Opus 4.6 is the budget
   anchor). Inline pattern, NOT the Makefile `census-run` target (that
   target depends on the dead `census` sweep):

   ```bash
   for i in 1 2 3 4; do
     uv run --project .. --env-file ../.env python -m aedist.worker openrouter --drain &
   done
   wait
   ```

   Monitor done/failed/spend live. Expected wall time 15–30 minutes.

4. `make -C experiments rebuild-measurements` to ingest the 85 records into
   `measurements.jsonl`. All should land with `prompt_version = "p1_base"`,
   `seed=42`, `max_tokens=32768`.

5. **Spot-check 3 runs** per the original 0177 exit criteria:
   - highest F1 (verify table is plausible),
   - lowest non-null F1 (diagnose failure mode),
   - one parse-error / refusal / `finish_reason=length` (classify).
   Record findings in this ticket log.

## Budget rules

- HARD LIMIT: `budget_usd=15` per the sweep config. The per-job
  `BudgetTracker` enforces it per-call; total spend is the sum across
  85 calls and must be tracked out-of-band.
- If total spend > $12 at <70% complete: halt, post a cost-table comment,
  escalate.
- If a single model accounts for >40% of spend: check `finish_reason` and
  response content for that model (length-truncation / loop pathology).
  Expected anchor: Opus 4.6 (~$0.20–0.40 per run, 5 reps × ~$1–2 total).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] 85 run files in `experiments/outputs/ablation/direct/p1_base/`,
      one per (model × rep) for the 17 journal models × 5 reps.
- [ ] All 85 entries in `measurements.jsonl` with `prompt_version = "p1_base"`
      and `seed = 42`.
- [ ] Refusal / parse-error / `finish_reason=length` counts logged here.
- [ ] Total spend logged here.
- [ ] Spot-check passed (3 runs reviewed: high-F1, low-F1, parse-error /
      length-truncation).
- [ ] No deletion of 0177 or rewrite of 0177 history — 0177 remains as the
      halted predecessor for provenance.

## Notes

- 0177 will be closed by a follow-up commit on this branch (or by the
  agent that lands the spot-checks) with reason "supplanted by 0181 —
  rerun on corrected 17-model journal set after PRs #338 / #341 / #346".
  Do not close 0177 in this ticket's commit — close it in the commit
  that lands the 85 measurements, so the closure carries the evidence.

- 0178 (manuscript update) consumes 0181's measurements directly. The
  manuscript annex must note the 0175→0180→0181 chain: original lock,
  set revision, rerun. PR #346's commit message and the open `tickets/0180`
  (rename ablation→exp1) capture the upstream context.

- 0181 carries no Blocked-by because all blockers are merged. If the
  user wants the rerun to wait on any further upstream change, add
  Blocked-by manually.
